            <div xml:id="d42">

                <pb facs="0101" n="27" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg27"/>

                <head>Mr. Burnley to Mr. Seward</head>
                <p rendition="#center">[Memorandum.]</p>
                <p>Relative to the apprehended attempts of persons hostile to the United States from
                    Canada, Viscount Monck informs me that he has taken measures for the prevention
                    of such acts, by the establishment of a detective police force, under special
                    stipendiary magistrates, along the border between Canada and the territory of
                    the United States.</p>
                <p>Viscount Monck has also called out for permanent duty a strong force of the
                    volunteer militia, who are to be stationed on the frontier line.</p>
                <p>These measures Viscount Monck hopes will effectually prevent any such attempts as
                    those alluded to.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">British
                            Legation</hi>, <placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1864-12-26"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 26,
                        1864</date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
